sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as Auditor / Reviewer
    participant WebUI as Web UI (Viewer, Webforms, AI Controls)
    participant Auth as Auth Service
    participant Session as Session Service
    participant Renderer as Renderer Service
    participant WAL as Workpaper Authoring Service (WAL)
    participant TMG as Template and Methodology Governance (TMG)
    participant Prompt as Prompt Management Service
    participant AgentReg as Agent Registry Service
    participant AgentOrch as Agent Orchestrator
    participant AgentRun as Agent Runtime
    participant FuncReg as Function Registry and Tools
    participant Memory as Common Memory Service
    participant DataIF as Data Interface
    participant Canonical as Canonical NoSQL DB
    participant DocExport as Document Export Service
    participant ObjectStore as Object Storage
    participant EventBus as Central Event Bus
    participant Audit as Immutable Audit Trail
    participant Usage as Usage Analytics (Kibana)
    participant Comment as Comment Service
    participant Review as Review Workflow Service

    %% 1. User logs in
    User->>WebUI: 1. Click Login
    WebUI->>Auth: 2. Send credentials
    Auth->>Auth: 3. Validate credentials
    Auth->>Session: 4. Issue session token and user context
    Session-->>WebUI: 5. Return session token and context
    WebUI-->>User: 6. Show authenticated UI

    %% 2. Render specific workpaper version
    User->>WebUI: 7. Request render of workpaper (docId, version, context)
    WebUI->>Renderer: 8. Request render (docId, version, context)
    Renderer->>WAL: 9. Fetch workpaper instance and version metadata
    WAL->>WAL: 10. Retrieve versioned structured content
    WAL->>TMG: 11. Request template schema and presentation model
    TMG-->>Renderer: 12. Return template schema and layout
    Renderer->>Renderer: 13. Apply schema, assemble view
    Renderer-->>WebUI: 14. Return rendered page (versioned)
    WebUI-->>User: 15. Display workpaper version

    %% 3. User captures audit data via webforms into canonical data
    User->>WebUI: 16. Fill webform fields (context: businessProcess, activity, subActivity)
    WebUI->>WAL: 17. Save structured updates (documentId, version, user, context)
    WAL->>WAL: 18. Create new immutable version (versionNumber++)
    WAL->>WAL: 19. Persist version to WAL_DB
    WAL->>EventBus: 20. Emit event WorkpaperVersionCreated (workpaperId, version)
    EventBus->>Audit: 21. Append event to immutable audit trail
    EventBus->>Usage: 22. Emit telemetry event (user action, time, context)
    WebUI-->>User: 23. Confirm save and show new version

    %% 4. User requests AI assistance for subsection
    User->>WebUI: 24. Click "AI Assist" on subsection
    WebUI->>Prompt: 25. Request prompt template selection (context)
    Prompt-->>WebUI: 26. Return prompt template id and placeholders
    WebUI->>AgentOrch: 27. Request prompt resolution (promptId, context, placeholders)
    AgentOrch->>DataIF: 28. Query data by context (documentId, version, businessProcess)
    DataIF->>Canonical: 29. Retrieve canonical data (fields, references)
    Canonical-->>DataIF: 30. Return data
    DataIF-->>AgentOrch: 31. Return resolved data
    AgentOrch->>Prompt: 32. Fill placeholders in prompt template with resolved data
    AgentOrch->>AgentRun: 33. Invoke agent runtime with resolved prompt (human-in-loop)
    AgentRun->>FuncReg: 34. Call function/tool if needed (evidence assembly, lookups)
    FuncReg-->>AgentRun: 35. Return tool outputs
    AgentRun->>Memory: 36. Read/write session memory as needed
    AgentRun-->>AgentOrch: 37. Return AI suggestion (draft text, summary)
    AgentOrch-->>WebUI: 38. Present suggestion to user (editable, flagged AI)
    WebUI-->>User: 39. Show AI suggestion for review

    %% 5. User accepts AI suggestion and system saves changes
    User->>WebUI: 40. Accept suggestion (or edit then accept)
    WebUI->>WAL: 41. Save accepted changes as new version (AI-assisted flag)
    WAL->>WAL: 42. Persist new version to WAL_DB
    WAL->>EventBus: 43. Emit event AIAssistedVersionCreated (workpaperId, version, promptId)
    EventBus->>Audit: 44. Append AI interaction event to audit trail
    EventBus->>Usage: 45. Emit AI usage telemetry

    %% 6. User requests AI agent to generate test plan
    User->>WebUI: 46. Click "Generate Test Plan"
    WebUI->>AgentReg: 47. Request agent instantiation (agent template: TestPlanAgent)
    AgentReg-->>AgentOrch: 48. Register and instruct orchestrator to create agent
    AgentOrch->>AgentRun: 49. Provision agent runtime (Langraph flow)
    AgentRun->>DataIF: 50. Pull control and evidence data by context
    AgentRun->>FuncReg: 51. Use MCP tools to assemble test steps
    AgentRun->>Memory: 52. Store session context and partial outputs
    AgentRun-->>AgentOrch: 53. Return proposed test plan (human-in-loop)
    AgentOrch-->>WebUI: 54. Present test plan to user for review

    %% 7. User finalizes and triggers document generation
    User->>WebUI: 55. Click "Generate Document" (PDF/Word)
    WebUI->>DocExport: 56. Request document generation (workpaperId, version, templateLayout)
    DocExport->>Renderer: 57. Request canonical render for specified version
    Renderer->>WAL: 58. Fetch versioned content
    WAL-->>Renderer: 59. Return content
    Renderer->>DocExport: 60. Return rendered artifact (PDF/Word)
    DocExport->>ObjectStore: 61. Store artifact and compute integrity hash
    ObjectStore-->>DocExport: 62. Return storage location and hash
    DocExport->>EventBus: 63. Emit ExportCreated event (artifactId, hash)
    EventBus->>Audit: 64. Append export event and integrity record
    EventBus->>Usage: 65. Emit export telemetry

    %% 8. User downloads and local save
    WebUI->>ObjectStore: 66. Request artifact download (artifactId)
    ObjectStore-->>WebUI: 67. Return artifact stream
    WebUI-->>User: 68. Trigger local save (download)

    %% 9. Collaboration events and review decisions
    User->>Comment: 69. Add comment anchored to field/version
    Comment->>EventBus: 70. Emit CommentAdded event
    EventBus->>Audit: 71. Append comment event
    User->>Review: 72. Submit review decision (approve / changes required)
    Review->>WAL: 73. If changes required, request WAL to transition lifecycle
    WAL->>EventBus: 74. Emit WorkpaperStatusChanged event
    EventBus->>Audit: 75. Append status change event

    %% 10. Analytics and dashboards
    EventBus->>Usage: 76. Stream events for projections
    Usage->>Usage: 77. Build KPIs and dashboards (Kibana)
    Usage-->>Leadership: 78. Visualize metrics (rework cycles, AI adoption)

    %% 11. End of flow
    Note over Audit, Usage: All events are immutable and reconstructable for lineage and verification